# Raw per-image data is regenerated/updated by the collector on every scheduled
# run and grows unbounded - it does NOT belong in git history (GitHub hard-blocks
# any file over 100MB, and repos aren't built for continuously-growing datasets
# like this anyway). It's persisted across CI runs via actions/cache instead - see
# .github/workflows/collect.yml.
#
# Only the small aggregate outputs (data/latest.json, data/history/*.json) that
# the dashboard actually reads get committed to git.

data/monthly/*.jsonl
data/monthly/*.csv
data/images_master.jsonl
data/images_master.jsonl.tmp
data/latest_images.csv

# Keep the tiny .done marker files though (they're just checkpoints, negligible size)
!data/monthly/*.done

# The chunked exports (data/monthly_chunks/*.csv, data/latest_images_chunks/*.csv)
# ARE committed to git - each part is kept under GitHub's size limit by
# src/export_chunks.py, so they're intentionally NOT ignored here.
